        "Content": "No. 74 Shrewsbury Park is situated in one of Dublin’s most desirable addresses, \r\na quiet, exclusive gated development, conveniently located off Merrion Road. This address offers residents the opportunity to enjoy all the entertainment, sporting and recreational amenities the city has to offer, yet live nearby in a quiet, private and secluded development.\r\n\r\nThis lovely 3-bedroomed end of Terrace home is deceptively spacious, with accommodation extending to approximately 100 sq m. The property offers generous proportions with accommodation briefly comprising entrance hall with guest bathroom, utility/cloakroom, reception/living room, kitchen and dining room on the ground floor. The first floor features three bedrooms (master en-suite) and bathroom. Outside to the front is a cobble-lock driveway, with off-street parking, to the rear is a walled garden, planted with mature shrubs and trees, which is not overlooked to the rear.\r\nBallsbridge has excellent transport links, including Sydney Parade & Sandymount Dart Stations which are only a short walk away and many bus routes to the City Centre /Southside.\r\n\r\nJust a short walk to Ballsbridge, Donnybrook and Sandymount villages. There are lots of amenities nearby including the Aviva Stadium, RDS Showgrounds, Fitzwilliam Tennis Club, Elm Park Golf Club, Herbert Park, St Vincent's Hospital and the Merrion Shopping Centre.\r\n\r\nThere are a wide array of Schools and Colleges nearby including nearby St Michaels College, Blackrock College, St Conleth’s College, Muckross Park, UCD and Trinity College Dublin.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway:  Wooden front door with stain glass insert, carpet, ceiling coving, alarm panel. \r\n\r\nGuest WC (1.32m x 0.96m):  Toilet, wash hand basin, carpet, vanity mirror and tiled splashback.\r\n\r\nUtility/cloakroom: Plumbed for washing machine. Understairs storage\r\n\r\nSitting Room (4.82m x 4.25m): Light-filled space benefitting from 2 front facing windows including a large bay window, wooden gas fireplace, carpet, ceiling coving, centre rose with chandelier.\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen: (2.26 m x 4.34m): Fully fitted modern kitchen units and counter top, with built-in Zanussi hob & electric oven, integrated fridge freezer, tiled floor, spotlights, breakfast bar, door to patio area and rear garden.\r\n\r\nDining Room (2.77m x 4.34m): Features full floor to ceiling glass, maximizing bright light and rear garden views. Potential to combine the Kitchen and Dining room into one large room, ceiling coving, carpet. \r\n\r\nUpstairs:\r\nMaster Bedroom (4.82m x 4.25m): Front aspect, featuring 2 large windows, built-in wardrobes, carpet. \r\n\r\nEn-suite (1.65m x 2.56 max): Tiled floor, walk in Mira Elite electric shower, wash hand basin, vanity unit, mirror, vanity light, part tiled walls, toilet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (2.69m max x 3.78 m): Rear aspect, built-in wardrobes, carpet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (2.06m x 3.78m): Rear aspect, built in wardrobes, carpet.\r\n\r\nBathroom (1.65m x 1.90m): Bath with shower attachment, part tiled walls, wash hand basin, toilet, tiled floor.\r\n\r\nExterior:\r\n\r\nFront garden features off-street parking on a cobble lock driveway, flower bed, lawn with hedging both sides.\r\n\r\nRear garden: features a selection of mature hedging and shrubs, lawn and a patio area, offering a wonderful private and peaceful space, which is not overlooked to the rear. Garden shed.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\n\r\n“Chain-Free” sale, the property is ready to go.\r\nSecure gated development\r\nSpacious 3 bedroom end of Terrace home, extends to approximately 100 sq.m\r\nSuperb much sought after residential address in Dublin 4\r\nQuiet cul-de-sac location\r\nOff-street parking\r\nAlarmed\r\nDouble glazed windows & doors\r\nMaster bedroom en-suite\r\nGuest toilet\r\nGas fired central heating\r\nNot overlooked at the rear of the property.\r\n\r\nBER Details\r\nBER: D\r\n\r\n\r\nDirections\r\nPostcode: D04C9K8\r\nFrom the City Centre, proceed along the Merrion Road, past the junction to Shrewsbury Road (on the right hand side), take the next turn left, follow to the end of the road, to the electric gated entrance of Shrewsbury Park. On entering the development, follow the road around to the end of the development. No 74 is in the line of houses at the end of the development.\r\n\r\nViewing Details;\r\nStrictly by Appointment\r\nPlease contact:\r\nJohn Fitzsimons  Fitzsimons Property  087 2204891  info@fitzsimonsproperty.ie   \r\n\r\nTo include:\r\nOven & hob, integrated fridge/freezer, garden shed\r\n\r\nJoint Agent;\r\nDowling Property Contact John J. Dowling 012118222  (PSL:002325)\r\n\r\nDisclaimer\r\nThese particulars are issued by Fitzsimons Property on the understanding that any negotiations relating to the property are conducted through them. While every care is taken in preparing these particulars, the firm does not hold themselves responsible for any inaccuracy in the particulars or the terms of the properties referred to or for any expense that maybe incurred in visiting same should it prove unsuitable or to have been let, sold or withdrawn. The purchaser is advised to make their own arrangements to satisfy themselves with measurements, details and contents included."
      }
